<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="1">

  <Content>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="0" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="AllCaps">FAde in:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="2/8" Page="1" Title=""/>
      <Text>Ext. Suburbia - subdivision street - day</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>An idyllic subdivision with crisp, well-kept lawns and rows of mailboxes lining the street rolls out into the distance.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Suddenly, a car rumbles through, disrupting the quaint stillness.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="7/8" Page="1" Title=""/>
      <Text>INT. Suburbia - Chloe’s car - Cont’D</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>CHLOE, 27, has a cellphone pressed between her ear and shoulder as she wrenches the rearview mirror into a position where she can see her face.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She pulls out lipstick from her purse on the passenger seat as she chats on the phone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHLOE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I was ready to give up on Craigslist, then wouldn’t you know, I get a job offer!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Chloe’s Dad (O.S.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(Over the phone)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>So what are you doing again?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHLOE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Part-time personal assistant to some actress. Uh, </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">Scarlette</Text>
      <Text> Hayes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chloe applies lipstick as she hurtles through the subdivision.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Chloe’s Dad (o.s.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>The old child star? One half of </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">Scarlette</Text>
      <Text> and Sophia?! Really?!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHLOE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Oh, so she really was world famous? The job listing read more delusional that factual.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Chloe’s Dad (o.S.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Their little sister act practically owned Broadway in the </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">80’s</Text>
      <Text>. The Sisters Hayes, they were called.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I wonder what they’re up to these days.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="2" Title=""/>
      <Text>INT. HayES RESIDENCE - Foyer - Cont’d</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The door creaks open as Chloe pokes her head in. She faintly knocks on the door while nervously looking around.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Chloe</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(cautiously)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Hello?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She gets no response as she cautiously enters the house, closing the door slowly behind her. When the door finally closes it still makes a pronounced CLANG as it latches.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chloe surveys the house. A modest dwelling, not too gaudy, but the walls are covered in pictures and framed clippings.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She moves towards a room across the foyer. She glances at the photos as she walks. She sees young, fresh faced girls and older men in tuxedos with beaming smiles.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>There’s a framed Playbill of an old Broadway play that Chloe had never heard of below a large one-sheet promoting The Sisters Hayes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <SceneProperties Length="2 7/8" Page="2" Title=""/>
      <Text>Int. Hayes resIDENCE - LIVING ROOM - Cont’d</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chloe enters the living room and notices SOPHIA, 47, sitting in a chair near the corner of the living room. A floor to ceiling bookshelf lines the wall behind her.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>On the wall next to Sophia are two framed child-sized sequined dresses.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chloe notices that Sophia is lost in thought.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHLOE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Hello?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>My name is Chloe, I’m </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">Scarlette’s</Text>
      <Text> new personal assistant.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Sophia doesn’t register.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHLOE (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You... You must be Sophie?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Sophia snaps out of her gaze and turns to Chloe.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Sophia</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(tersely)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Sophia.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chloe recoils slightly from the icy retort.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CHLOE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Oh, I’m sorry, Sophia.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It’s a pleasure to meet you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chloe extends her hand. Sophia stands and holds out a limp hand for Chloe to awkwardly shake.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SOPHIA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Charmed. I’m sure.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Sophia looks Chloe up and down.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SopHIA (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Tea?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chloe nods and Sophia exits.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Sophia (o.S.) (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(shouting)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>So you’re </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">Scarlette’s</Text>
      <Text> new slave?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chloe turns to look at the dresses on the wall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ChLOE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1" Background="#FFFFFFFFFFFF" Color="#000000000000" Font="Courier Final Draft" RevisionID="0" Size="12" Style="">Umm</Text>
      <Text>... Well, assistant.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She continues surveying the room and comes across a table in front of the window that has a small collection of Hummel figurines.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chloe takes a closer look at the small trinkets, amazed at their artistry. The small children’s faces looking on with such doe-eyed wonder, Chloe catches herself smiling as she gazes at them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SOPHIA (o.S.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(shouting)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I’m messing with you, my dear!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She reaches out to pick one up for a closer look.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Holding one in her hand, she flips it around, looking at the small details on the piece.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Sophia enters the room carrying a tray with a tea pot and two tea cups on it. Her face snaps from a practiced smile to dread when she sees Chloe holding the figurine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Sophia (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(insistently)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>PUT THAT DOWN!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Sophia’s booming command startles Chloe, which causes her to jump in fright making her drop the figurine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Sophia watches the small trinket fall. Her mouth widens as the figurine descends to the hardwood floor. The trinket shatters making Sophia drop the tea tray. The cacophony of SHATTERING is intensified as Sophia dashes past Chloe to the broken pieces of her beloved Hummel figurine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chloe stands behind Sophia and attempts to mumble an apology.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SOPHIA (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Frederick! You killed Frederick!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Sophia drops to her knees surveying the pieces. She’s nearly hyperventilating as she begins to scoop the shards of porcelain into her hands.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>One sharp piece cuts Sophia’s hand, which she doesn’t even register as she hurries to scoop together every last piece.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Her blood begins to coat each piece as she brings them to the tabletop, resting them like a fallen comrade in front of the other figurines.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chloe looks on in regret.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Chloe</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I’m so sorry, Sophia.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Sophia is caught in a one-sided conversation with the figurines.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SOPHIA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>But, she didn’t know any better, Frederick...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I... I’m sorry... She’s...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(beat)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Yes. Yes, I understand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ChLOE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It obviously meant a lot to you. Is there anything I can do?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chloe’s words enrage Sophia. She turns to look over her shoulder. Her eyes burning with anger.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Sophia</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Is there anything you can do?!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Sophia stands to her feet and turns square with Chloe.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>Sophia (CONT’D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Yes... There is something...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Chloe takes a step back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>ChLOe</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>What?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Sophia charges at Chloe. Chloe screams and is quickly silenced by Sophia’s grasp around her neck.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition">
      <Text>SMASH TO BLACK:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>SOPHIA (v.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Blood for blood.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>TITLE CARD: THE SISTERS HAYES</Text>
    </Paragraph>
  </Content>

